the interception of ryanair flight 4978  is now a full-blown international  diplomatic crisis  belarus state media says president  lukashenko personally ordered a military  jet  to escort the passenger plane away from  its scheduled route  and diverted to minsk it's an act which  european leaders have branded  state-sponsored piracy  and there is now intense pressure for a  stern response  flight tracker sites showed the ryanair  flight from athens to vilnius  changed course just two minutes from the  lithuanian border  belarus air traffic control had flagged  a supposed bomb alert to the aircraft  then scrambled a fighter jet to make  doubly sure  the plane came to minsk the target of  the extraordinary intervention was this  man  roman protesovic an opposition  journalist and blogger  who fled belarus after president  lukashenko claimed victory in last  august disputed election  fellow passengers on the plane say he  reacted to the interception  first with disbelief and then  resignation one minute he was a  like trying to negotiate with a steward  but nothing to do but after that  i didn't find him a scared or hungry or  something like that  the incident will dominate the summit of  european leaders gathering in brussels  later on monday  nato will consider its response when it  meets on tuesday  there are demands for yet more sanctions  against lukashenko and his closest  officials  as well as calls to suspend all transit  from belarus into the eu  lukashenko is sort of testing the  uh the tolerance of the eu showing  uh that uh he can get along with even at  the background of a strange relations  with the west  and being under sanctions and  condemnation and his legitimacy is not  recognized by eu  leadership he can still make this  powerful moves  prosecute his opponents even those who  managed to  escape belarus alexander lukashenko has  been belarus president since 1994  a leader described in some quarters as  europe's last dictator  and a man who has a record of harshly  repressing dissent but he is strongly  supported  by his ally russia he is uh  playing his trump card saying that we  together with russia against the west  against hypocrisy and imperialism  and that's what he's playing and uh he  is playing this card in order to ensure  uh russian support russian money and  russian influence  in light of very mild and very uh  appeasing sanctions of european union  america  it's now known that 125 passengers  departed from athens and only 121  arrived in vilnius lending credence to  reports that protacovich had been  followed onto the plane by belarus  intelligence agents  the midair interception is looking less  and less like an opportunistic act  and more like a planned and coordinated  snatch operation  and the dilemma for the west is how to  respond to that  paul brennan al jazeera
 

